It creates a unique owner (namesakeCount 0) with an email, maxing the two pre-tenure factors (1 + 1 email + 1 unique = 3), and asserts `membershipLevel == 3` — verifying the level-4/tenure cap.

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceBase.java` — the black-box base class providing the helpers this test uses: `ownerNode()` (lines 117-125, a fully-unique owner so namesakeCount stays 0), `withPostcode()` (129-132), `uniqueEmail()` (106-108), `createOwnerOk()` (160-162), `getOwner()` (189-191). It is `@Transactional` (rolled back per test) and authenticates as a mock admin.

No dedicated unit tests exist for `AssignOwnerMembershipLevel`, `AssignOwnerNamesakeCount`, `AssignOwnerHousehold`, `AssignOwnerHouseholdSize`, or `Household` — coverage is only through the acceptance test above.

